── a view is a function → hiccup → HTML ──

  shorthand :main#app.board
    <main id="app" class="board">hello</main>
  attrs + class merge
    <div class="card active" data-role="admin">x</div>
  a task list (for splices)
    <ul><li class="task" data-key="a">First</li><li class="task" data-key="b">Second</li></ul>
  escaping + event marker
    <button data-ev-click='["intent","go",{}]'>Save &amp; &lt;exit&gt;</button>

  the shape of it: a view is data. No template, no DSL — a function
  you can call, print, and test with =. Everything else builds on this.
── the diff is minimal, and keyed ──

  one text change, deep — one op at a path
    ops: [[:text [0 0 0] "new"]]
  append a keyed row — one :insert, not a re-render
    ops: [[:insert [] "b" 1 [:li {:key "b"} "B"]]]
  remove a keyed row — one :remove
    ops: [[:remove [] "a"]]
  reorder three rows — :move ops, DOM nodes preserved
    ops: [[:move [] "c" 0]]

── the diff round-trips: apply(diff(a,b), a) == b ──
  reconstruct == target? true

  the shape of it: minimal, keyed patches. A reorder moves nodes
  instead of rewriting them — the property a string diff cannot reach.
── a view is a value you can assert on ──

  tree is a vector? true
  root tag: main
  role attr: admin
  renders two rows? true
  guest role: guest

  the shape of it: no socket, no browser, no server. A view is a
  function from a database value to data — unit-testable in full.
